@startuml 00-context
' =====================================================================
'  HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN — System Context (C4 Level 1)
'  Nexo — Cloud-native 5G Core management platform
' =====================================================================
title Nexo Platform — System Context (HLD / C4-L1)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #444444
  roundCorner 12
}
left to right direction

actor "Platform Admin"     as ADMIN
actor "Network Operator"   as OPER
actor "Security Analyst"   as ANALYST
actor "Auditor"            as AUDIT

rectangle "**Nexo Platform**\nSpring Boot microservices + Angular 22 console\nRBAC · Observability · Roaming analytics" as NEXO #E8F0FE

rectangle "Keycloak\nOAuth2 / OIDC Identity Provider\nrealm: auth-management" as KC #FEF7E0
rectangle "free5GC + UERANSIM\n(external 5G Core substrate,\nseparate Linux runtime)" as CORE #E6F4EA
rectangle "SMTP (Gmail)\nOTP + temp-password mail" as MAIL #FCE8E6
rectangle "Observability Backends\nPrometheus · Grafana · Loki · Tempo" as OBS #F3E8FD

ADMIN   --> NEXO : manage users, roles,\nplatform config, health
OPER    --> NEXO : view/restart NFs,\napply core config
ANALYST --> NEXO : roaming analytics,\nanomalies, rate-limit policies
AUDIT   --> NEXO : read-only,\naudit logs

NEXO --> KC   : authenticate (password grant),\nvalidate JWT, admin REST
NEXO ..> CORE : consume NF metrics / logs /\nsignalling (roadmap: /api/nf/*)
NEXO --> MAIL : send OTP / temp passwords
NEXO --> OBS  : export metrics / logs / traces

note bottom of NEXO
  Every user reaches the platform through ONE door (the API Gateway :9000).
  Authorization is permission-based (PERM_*), decoupled from role names.
end note

@enduml
